  The consequence beyond that line: this is a session lifetime, so it's a security-posture change. A 16x extension means
  a stolen session token, an unlocked laptop, or a shared/kiosk browser stays usable for a full working day instead of
  half an hour, and idle sessions no longer self-expire within a work session.

